SUMMARY:A narrowly missed four-body resonant chain among the Galilean moons
DESCRIPTION:The Galilean moons of Jupiter present one of the most peculiar 
 orbital configurations in the solar system: a 4:2:1 three-body resonance b
 etween Io\, Europa\, and Ganymede\, known as Laplace resonance. The outer 
 moon\, Callisto\, is not involved in the Laplace resonance\, but it is cur
 rently very close to a 7:3 resonance with Ganymede. Considering the estima
 ted rate of the moons' orbital migration…\nhttps://indico.obspm.fr/event
 /3428/
LOCATION:PARIS
